We need to isolate the variable [MATH: x.] To do this, we treat [MATH: y] as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.

In this case, we simply divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 4\mathbin{:}]

[MATH: \eqalign{
\require{cancel}
4x &= y \[5pt]
\dfrac {4x} {4} &= \dfrac y 4 \[5pt]
\dfrac {{\cancel{4}}x} {\cancel{4}} &= \dfrac y 4 \[5pt]
x &= \dfrac y4
}]
